WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.350
Run the power rule down a list.

2
00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:05.820
x squared integrates
to x cubed over three.

3
00:00:05.870 --> 00:00:08.820
x integrates to x squared over two.

4
00:00:08.870 --> 00:00:11.530
x to the nought integrates to x.

5
00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:15.270
Next: x to the minus one, one over x.

6
00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:17.110
And the rule jams.

7
00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:22.030
Yet y equals one over x is a
smooth curve with area beneath it.

8
00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:24.460
So why does its integral give a logarithm,

9
00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:25.880
not a power?

10
00:00:25.930 --> 00:00:28.380
In this mission, you'll
see where the power rule,

11
00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:32.070
x to the n plus one
over n plus one, fails.

12
00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:35.770
You'll use integration as the
reverse of differentiation.

13
00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:40.390
And you'll hunt for a function you
know whose derivative is one over x.

14
00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:44.970
Your mission: explain why integrating
one over x gives a logarithm,

15
00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:45.950
not a power.
